values ('d8e9f0a1-2b3c-4e18-9f78-8a9b0c1d2e88', 'research-methods-in-anthropology', 'Research Methods in Anthropology', 'Research methods in anthropology are a disciplined way of producing accountable knowledge about human life, combining interpretive, comparative, historical, and empirical habits of inquiry. Students design questions and fieldsites, practice ethics and reflexivity, and collect evidence through observation, interviews, elicitation, surveys, archives, and material or digital methods, then analyze, steward, and write that evidence into a feasible project.');

